  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Why it matters",
    body:
        "The flam accent is the triplet with a backbone: a heavy first note, two light ones. It teaches hands to change roles every beat, flam, tap, tap, with the lead switching sides.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "How to play it",
    body:
        "lR L R, then rL R L, as eighth-note triplets. The flam is loud (accent), the two taps are low and even.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Practice tips",
    body:
        "Keep the taps really low, the contrast is the point. Line 3 moves the three-note group onto sixteenths, so the accents drift across the beats, line 7 turns it into a shuffle.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Where you hear it",
    body:
        "Marching and drum corps music, swing drummers phrasing in threes, the 12/8 blues ballad where every beat has a weighted first note.",
